[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me reconsider the problem. I think the problem is asking about the[0m[38;2;124;124;124mgeneral profinite case, where the order is the supernatural number $l \cdot p^n$[0m[38;2;124;124;124mwith $n$ possibly infinite.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this more carefully. For profinite groups, the Sylow theorems[0m[38;2;124;124;124mhave analogs. A $p$-Sylow subgroup of a profinite group $G$ is a maximal pro-$p$[0m[38;2;124;124;124msubgroup, and its index is coprime to $p$ (in the supernatural number sense).[0m

